  <!-- Iteration -->
  <section class="case-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Iteration</p>
      <h2>Simplicity under complexity</h2>
      <p>My first iterations let users filter flights by "earlier" or "later" to narrow the list quickly. I pushed to keep the UI simple. Someone making a snap decision at the airport should not face a learning curve. I also pushed to show flight details and boarding status directly in the results, so travelers understood the implications of their new flight before committing.</p>
      <p>Behind that simple interface sat dozens of business rules, DOT regulations, and edge cases (party splitting logic, seat transfer validation, and more). The design job was to absorb all of that so the traveler never had to.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

